<asp:Content ID="Content3" ContentPlaceHolderID="ContentPlaceHolder2" runat="server">
    
    <div id="MainBox">
        <h2>
            Goku is quite possibly the most iconic and recognizable anime character of all time. He is <br>
            everything that shonen anime heroes aspire to be and more, setting the standard for what a <br>
            great anime protagonist should be. Goku is kind, pure-hearted, and strong, making him the <br>
            ideal heroic character.
        </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="textBoxes" id="box1">
        <h2>
            After landing on planet Earth, Goku is found by a hermit named Gohan living in the forest, 
            who takes Goku in and raises him as his own grandson. At first, Goku is difficult to handle as 
            he is prone to acting out, but after suffering a traumatic head injury that puts him into a coma, 
            Goku wakes up having completely forgotten his previous identity and has a much calmer disposition.
        </h2>
        <img id="spacepod1" src="/images/SpacePod.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box2">
        <h2>
            Goku then lives with his Grandpa for several more years in peace. Sadly, when <br>
            Goku is around 10 years old, he is transformed into his Oozaru form in a full moon and <br>
            accidentally kills his grandfather during his rampage. Goku then lives in the wilderness for a <br>
            few years before meeting a young girl named Bulma, who finds Goku while on a search for the <br>
            mystical Dragon Balls.
        </h2>
        <img id="kidGoku5" src="/images/kidGoku5.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box3">
        <h2>
            Realizing Goku is the holder of the four-star Dragon Ball, which he is <br>
            unwilling to part with, Bulma invites young Goku to join her on her search, thus beginning his <br>
            journey.
        </h2>
        <img id="KidGokuWithDragonBall" src="/images/KidGokuWithDragonBall.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box4">
        <h2>
            Shortly after meeting Bulma, Goku would go on to meet a number of other lifelong <br>
            companions during his journey to help Bulma find the Dragon Balls. Goku meets Master <br>
            Roshi the turtle hermit, who gives Bulma a Dragon Ball, Oolong, the creepy shapeshifting pig, <br>
            and Yamcha, a bandit who travels with his pal Pilar and who is cripplingly shy around women. <br>
            Goku also meets a young girl named Chichi, who lives near Fire Mountain with her dad, the Ox King.
        </h2>
        <img id="Roshi1" src="/images/Roshi1.png">
        <img id="oolong1" src="/images/oolong1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box5">
        <h2>
            In order to put out the fire on the mountain, Goku enlists the help of Master Roshi, who does <br>
            just that using his ultimate technique, the Kamehameha wave. Goku is shocked by the power <br>
             of this attack and manages to pull off the same move moments after witnessing Roshi use it, <br>
             much to the Turtle Hermit's shock. With six of the seven Dragon Balls in their possession, <br>
             Goku and his friends discover that the remaining Dragon Ball is held by Emperor Pilaf, a <br>
             villainous ruler who — with the help of his minions Mai and Shu — plans to gather the Dragon <br>
             Balls in hopes of making a wish to rule the world. Pilaf steals the Dragon Balls from Goku and <br>
             locks him away. However, just as Pilaf is about to make his wish, Oolong jumps in and makes <br>
             his own ridiculous wish instead, angering Pilaf. On the night before he and the others are due <br>
             to be executed by Pilaf, Goku breaks out of the prison with his Oozaru form. With another year <br>
             until Shenron can be summoned again, Goku agrees to train with Master Roshi to learn the 
             secrets of the Turtle School.
        </h2>
        <img id="pilaf1" src="/images/EmperorPilaf1.png">
        <img id="shu1" src="/images/Shu1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box6">
        <h2>
            Meeting Master Roshi, in particular, was a turning point in Goku's life. As a Saiyan, Goku <br>
            always had an innate desire for combat and a natural talent for it, but Roshi was the first one <br>
            to take him under his wing and guide Goku in the art of combat. During his training, Goku also <br>
            met Krillin, who would become his best friend well into their adulthood. To test his new skills, <br>
            Goku entered the 21st World Martial Arts Tournament, where he made it to the final round but lost <br>
            against Master Roshi, who had entered the tournament disguised as Jackie Chun.
        </h2>
        <img id="JackieChan1" src="/images/JackieChan1.png">
        <img id="kidKrillin2" src="/images/kidKrillin2.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box7">
        <h2>
            With Goku's training complete and the World Tournament behind him, Goku sets off to find his <br>
            Grandfather's Dragon Ball. His search leads him to get wrapped up in the dealings of a <br>
            terrifying criminal organization known as the Red Ribbon Army. During his travels, Goku meets <br>
            a young boy named Upa, whose father, Bora, was killed by the Red Ribbon Army. Goku decides to <br>
            regather all of the Dragon Balls in order to wish Bora back to life, and this results in a <br>
            difficult struggle against the Red Ribbon Army itself.
        </h2>
        <img id="Red_Ribbon_Army1" src="/images/Red_Ribbon_Army1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box8">
        <h2>
            During this time, Goku climbs to the top of Muscle Tower, escapes the powerful General Blue, <br>
            and faces off against the terrifying assassin Mercenary Tao. After losing to Tao, Goku climbs <br>
            Korin Tower to drink the mystical Sacred Water, which is said to give those who drink it great <br>
            powers. Goku soon learns that the true power he gained was from climbing the tower itself, and <br>
            his newfound strength allows him to take down Mercenary Tao in their rematch.
        </h2>
        <img id="korin1" src="/images/Korin1.png">
        <img id="tao1" src="/images/MercenaryTao2.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box9">
        <h2>
            Goku then goes on to singlehandedly destroy the Red Ribbon Army and acquire the Dragon Balls <br>
            they hold. However, there's still one more Dragon Ball missing, held by the mysterious witch, <br>
            Fortuneteller Baba. Goku defeats all of Baba's minions and is rewarded with the final Dragon <br>
            Ball, which he uses to resurrect Upa's father. Goku then spends the next few years traveling <br>
            the land and training for the 22nd Tenkaichi Budokai.
        </h2>
        <img id="FortunetellerBaba1" src="/images/FortunetellerBaba1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box10">
        <h2>
            After three years of traveling, Goku enters the tournament along with Krillin and Yamcha. <br>
            Goku's training definitely paid off, as he impresses Krillin in their fight together and easily <br> 
            defeats his other opponents. Goku makes it to the final round, where he faces Tien Shinhan of <br>
            the Crane School. After an evenly matched battle, Tien just barely wins due to a lucky incident, <br>
            but Goku gains Tien's respect as a warrior in the end.
        </h2>
        <img id="TienShinhan1" src="/images/TeinShinHan.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box11">
        <h2>
            After the tournament, Goku finds Krillin has been killed by the evil monster Tambourine, who <br>
            is one of the minions of the Demon King Piccolo. He proceeds to challenge the demon but is <br>
            defeated easily, showing that he still has room to grow before he can face King Piccolo. Goku <br>
            meets Yajirobe, a warrior with great strength of his own, and together, they defeat Krillin's <br>
            killer. This enrages King Piccolo, who shows up and defeats Goku, even believing he has killed him. <br>
        </h2>
        <img id="kingPiccolo" src="/images/kingPiccolo1.png">
        <img id="yajirobe1" src="/images/Yajirobe1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box12">
        <h2>
            Goku then climbs Korin Tower with Yajirobe and drinks the Ultra Sacred Water in order to <br>
            unlock his hidden potential. Newly invigorated, Goku teams up with Tien to face Piccolo again, <br>
            who has wished on the Dragon Balls to restore his true power and then killed Shenron after his <br>
            wish was granted. Even with Piccolo's increased power, Goku and Tien seem to have the upper <br>
            hand. However, King Piccolo captures Tien and threatens to take his life unless Goku surrenders.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box13">
        <img id="kidGokuWinPiccolo" src="/images/kidGokuWinPiccolo.jpg">
        <h2>
            Goku complies, and the demon king breaks three of Goku's limbs to render him helpless. In a <br>
            final effort, Goku uses a one-handed Kamehameha to launch himself from the ground toward King <br>
            Piccolo and bursts through the Demon King's abdomen with a one-handed punch, killing Piccolo <br>
            once and for all. With Piccolo's dying breath, he coughs up a giant egg, which later hatches, <br>
            revealing Piccolo's reincarnation: Piccolo Jr.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box14">
        <h2>
            After the fight with King Piccolo, Goku recovers at Korin Tower. Korin informs Goku that Kami <br>
            created the Dragon Balls and can thus recreate Shenron, so he instructs him to use his power <br>
            pole to reach Kami's lookout from Korin Tower. Once there, Kami agrees to recreate the Dragon <br>
            Balls under the condition that Goku trains at Kami's lookout with Mr. Popo to face Piccolo Jr. 
            in three years at the 23rd Tenkaichi Budokai.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box15">
        <h2>
            At the tournament, Goku reveals himself to look much older, much to the surprise of his old <br>
            friends. Goku swiftly makes his way through his opponents, one of whom is Chi-Chi, whom Goku <br>
            agrees to marry upon the conclusion of the tournament. After an intense battle, Goku defeats <br>
            Piccolo Jr. and shows him mercy by asking Kami to allow him to live. Named the new champion <br>
            and the world's strongest fighter, Goku flies off into the sunset with Chi-chi in his arms.
        </h2>
        <img id="gokuUmbrella" src="/images/gokuUmbrella.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box16">
        <h2>
            At the start of DBZ, Goku has started a family and made the Earth his home, though his heritage <br>
            as a Saiyan finally catches up to him and tests his resolve. Along the way, Goku will make <br>
            powerful friends who assist him in defeating the ever-growing existential threats sent to Earth. <br>
            Goku is married to Chi-Chi, and their first son, Gohan, is born. This proves to be a time of 
            Goku's growing family — in more ways than one.
        </h2>
        <img id="kidGohanBaby" src="/images/kidGohanBaby.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box17">
        <h2>
            Not only does Goku start a family with Chi-Chi, but he soon learns of his family heritage as <br>
            well. When Gohan is only 3 years old, Goku's older brother, Raditz, arrives on Earth, <br>
            threatening to destroy it unless Goku joins him. Goku refuses and teams up with Piccolo to stop <br>
            Raditz. In a last-ditch effort to destroy Raditz, Goku holds his brother down while Piccolo <br>
            fires his Special Beam Cannon, killing both Goku and Raditz in the process.
        </h2>
        <img id="Raditz1" src="/images/Raditz1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box18">
        <h2>
            Because of his good deeds on Earth, Goku is reborn in the Other World with his body still <br>
            intact, and he travels down Snake Way to train with King Kai for the next year. It takes him <br>
            88 days to reach King Kai's planet for the first time, though his return journey takes him <br>
            only one day after his considerable power boost.
        </h2>
        <img id="KingKai1" src="/images/KingKai1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box19">
        <h2>
            Just as predicted by Raditz, Vegeta and Nappa arrive on Earth after a year. Goku is then <br>
            revived by the Dragon Balls and arrives to find all of his friends in bad shape — including <br>
            Piccolo, who had given his life to protect Gohan. Goku fights and ultimately defeats Vegeta, <br>
            but like Piccolo Jr. before him, Vegeta is granted mercy by Goku, who allows the villain to 
            escape with his life.
        </h2>
        <img id="VegetaStartZ" src="/images/VegetaStartZ.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box20">
        <h2>
            After recovering in the hospital, Goku travels on a specially-made spaceship to Namek. Goku <br>
            trains in one hundred times gravity throughout the entire journey, causing him to grow even <br>
            stronger. Goku then arrives at the fight just in the nick of time to face the Ginyu Force and <br>
            protect his friends. After an initially straightforward fight that gets complicated due to <br>
            Ginyu's Body Swap ability, Goku takes down the Ginyu Force and finds himself face-to-face with Frieza.
        </h2>
        <img id="frizaDBZ" src="/images/frizaDBZ.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box21">
        <h2>
            Frieza proves too powerful for Goku, making a mockery of the Saiyan in their fight. He quickly <br>
            turns to injuring those around Goku, just to hurt his pride. In the process, Frieza kills <br>
            Krillin, which sends Goku into a rage, causing him to transform into the <span class="form">legendary Super Saiyan</span> . <br>
            Goku then toys with Frieza, definitively proving himself the superior fighter.
        </h2>
        <img id="GokuSjj3" src="/images/GokuSjj3.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box22">
        <h2>
            In desperation, Frieza fires an energy blast, which causes the planet to begin to crumble, <br>
            hoping to take Goku down with him. Goku defeats Frieza and then escapes from Namek in one of <br>
            the Ginyu's space pods. On his return journey, Goku stumbles upon the remote planet Yardrat, <br>
            where he trains for a brief time before traveling back to Earth.
        </h2>
        <img id="yardratGoku1" src="/images/yardratGoku1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box23">
        <h2>
            When he arrives back on Earth, Goku meets Future Trunks, who warns him of the coming arrival <br>
            of the Androids as well as his death due to a heart virus. Sure enough, three years later, <br>
            Goku faces off with Androids 19 and 20, as Trunks predicted. Additionally, as Trunks had also <br>
            warned him, Goku begins to succumb to his heart disease mid-fight. Goku spends the next ten <br>
            days recovering after receiving the antidote and awakens to find that the Earth is faced with <br>
            a new threat: Cell.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box24">
        <h2>
            Goku decides to train with Gohan in the hyperbolic time chamber for a day, during which time both <br>
            he and his son reach new levels of power. Goku fights Cell first in the Cell Games, and — despite <br>
            being stronger than the Android initially — his power quickly runs out while Cell's never does. <br>
            Goku eventually surrenders, and he even gives Cell a senzu bean in order to have him at full <br>
            strength to fight Gohan.
        </h2>
        <img id="cell2" src="/images/Cell2.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box25">
        <h2>
            When Cell recognizes he can't beat Gohan, he attempts to self-destruct and destroy the planet <br>
            along with him. In order to save the Earth from certain destruction, Goku uses his instant <br>
            transmission to teleport Cell to the farthest place he can think of from Earth: King Kai's planet.
        </h2>
        <img id="cellExplode1" src="/images/cellExplode1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box26">
        <h2>
            After Gohan defeats Cell for good, the group decides to revive Goku using the Dragon Balls, <br>
            but Goku refuses. Goku feels that he has been the cause of the increasingly powerful villains <br>
            who came to Earth looking for him and feels they'll be safer without him around. Besides, his <br>
            son already proved he was strong enough to protect the world in Goku's absence. So, instead of <br>
            being revived, Goku remains in the Other World, training with the Grand Kai and Pikkon.
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box27">
        <h2>
            Goku is granted one day on Earth to visit his family and take part in the 25th Tenkaichi <br>
            Budokai tournament. Though things begin as expected, things go south when Shin warns Goku <br>
            and the Z Fighters of Babidi's plan to revive Majin Buu. Goku goes with the others to stop <br>
            the evil wizard, but Vegeta succumbs to Babadi's mind control and the warriors are transported <br>
            back to the World Tournament stage. Goku and Majin Vegeta take part in an intense battle, <br>
            during which time Majin Buu is restored to full power and unsealed from his prison.
        </h2>
        <img id="majinVegeta" src="/images/MaginVegeta1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box28">
        <h2>
            Goku engages Buu with his new SSJ 3 form, much to Vegeta's surprise, but it wastes too much <br>
            power too quickly, and Goku is unable to finish the job. Later, Goku convinces Vegeta to fuse <br>
            with him using the Potara earrings, and the two become the <span class="form">powerful warrior Vegito</span>. Despite <br>
            gaining the upper hand, the Potara earrings wear off, and the two become separated again. <br>
            In a last-ditch attempt, Goku summons all his power into a final Spirt Bomb attack and uses it <br>
            to successfully destroy Kid Buu. Recognizing that Good Buu wasn't at fault, Goku uses the <br>
            Dragon Balls to wish for all of humanity to forget about what Buu did before so that he could <br>
            live on Earth in peace.
        </h2>
        <img id="kidBuu1" src="/images/kidBuu1.png">
        <img id="GokuSjj_3" src="/images/GokuSjj_3.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box29">
        <h2>
            Goku has already surpassed the Kami and Kais of his world during Dragon Ball Z, but he is in <br>
            for a divine surprise in the following years of Super. This period takes place between the end <br>
            of the Buu Saga and the beginning of DBZ's final arc. 
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box30">
        <h2>
            Following the death of Buu, Goku experiences a time of peace, during which he becomes a farmer <br>
            to make ends meet for his family. That peace is short-lived, however. During Bulma's birthday <br>
            party, the <span class="form">God of Destruction</span>, Beerus, arrives on planet Earth looking for the <span class="form"> "Super Saiyan <br>
            God."</span> Beerus is unimpressed by Goku's Super Saiyan transformation, so the group turns to Shenron for help.
        </h2>
        <img id="LordBeerus1" src="/images/LordBeerus1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box31">
        <h2>
            With the help of Shenron and five Saiyans, Vegeta, Gohan, Goten, Trunks, and the yet-to-be-born <br>
            Pan, Goku is transformed into the Super Saiyan god, and his fight with Beerus commences. <br>
            Goku has become so powerful that his blows with Beerus shake the fabric of the universe itself, <br>
            and Beerus takes such a liking to Goku that he agrees to allow Goku and Vegeta to train with the <br>
            angel Whis on his planet.
        </h2>
        <img id="GokuSjjGod2" src="/images/GokuSjjGod2.png">
        <img id="Shenron1" src="/images/Shenron1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box32">
        <h2>
            Goku and Vegeta's training with Whis ends up paying off when they are faced with the return of 
            an age-old threat: Frieza. Frieza shows off a <span class="form">powerful new Golden form</span>, but it ultimately isn't 
            enough to beat Goku and Vegeta in their new <span class="form">Super Saiyan Blue</span> transformations.
        </h2>
        <img id="Friza3" src="/images/Friza3.png">
        <img id="GokuAndVegeta" src="/images/GokuAndVegeta.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box33">
        <h2>
            After Frieza's defeat, Beerus gets into an argument with his brother, Champa, the God of <br>
            Destruction of Universe 6. The two declare a tournament to decide whose universe is stronger. <br>
            After a difficult battle against Hit, Goku proves victorious by combining his SSJ Blue with <br>
            Kaoiken. The <span class="form">all-powerful God Zeno</span> takes notice of this impromptu tournament and decides it <br>
            would be fun to host his own multiversal tournament with extremely high stakes: every universe <br>
            except the one that emerges victorious will be erased forever!
        </h2>
        <img id="hit1" src="/images/hit1.png">
        <img id="Zeno1" src="/images/Zeno1.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box34">
        <h2>
            With Zeno's tournament decided, a new threat suddenly arises for Universe 7. Future Trunks <br>
            arrives in his time capsule to seek help from Goku after a mysterious evil version of Goku <br>
            has attacked his world. This evil Goku, dubbed <span class="form">"Goku Black"</span>, turns out to be Zamasu, a Kai <br>
            who became evil and wished for Goku's power using the Super Dragon Balls. Goku goes with Vegeta <br>
            to Trunks' time to help stop Goku Black, but he proves far too powerful, and the three Saiyans <br>
            are forced to retreat back to the present twice. Only after combining with Vegeta using the <br>
            potara earrings to become <span class="form">Vegito</span> do the Z Warriors finally see a light at the end of the tunnel. <br>
            In the end, it takes Zeno to erase Zamasu and rescue Trunks' future.
        </h2>
        <img id="GokuBlack1" src="/images/GokuBlack1.png">
        <img id="VegitoSjjBlue" src="/images/VegitoSjjBlue.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box35">
        <h2>
            With Zamasu defeated, Goku and Vegeta make it back to the present just in time to begin <br>
            training and gathering the team of fighters joining them in Zeno's Tournament of Power. Goku <br>
            recruits most of the usual suspects but reserves one final spot for Frieza, whom he offers to <br>
            revive in exchange for fighting alongside Universe 7. It takes some convincing, but Frieza <br>
            accepts, and the group is transported to the custom stadium created for the universal tournament.
        </h2>
        <img id="TOParena" src="/images/TOParena.png">
    </div>
    <div class="textBoxes" id="box36">
        <h2>
            Goku faces off against incredible fighters in the TOP's battle royale, including a rematch <br>
            against Hit and a fight with Universe 6's powerful Saiyans Kale and Caulifla. Most notable <br>
            among Goku's enemies during the TOP is Jiren, <span class="form">a warrior so strong that Goku is powerless <br>
            against him even in his SSJ Blue state.</span> When all hope seems lost, Goku taps into a power that <br>
            even Beerus has yet to master: <span class="form">Ultra Instinct!</span> This technique of the gods gives Goku the edge <br>
            he needs to equal and even surpass Jiren's power, but it doesn't last long. It's only through <br>
            the combined effort of Goku, Android 17, and Frieza that Universe 7 is able to pull through and <br>
            save the multiverse.
        </h2>
        <img id="Giren1" src="/images/Giren1.png">
        <img id="GokuUi2" src="/images/GokuUi2.png">
    </div>

    <img id="AllTheGang" src="/images/AllTheGang.png">
    <img id="GokuPoseHi" src="/images/GokuPoseHi.png">
    <h1 id="myH1">Goku</h1>
